              ToolMessage(content='I\'ve completed my search (12 searches). Based on my research, here are the best wedding venue options in Paris for 100 guests, ranked by the balance of price, exact capacity, and reviews:\n\n## 🏆 Best Overall Options\n\n### 1. La Fabrique République (10th arr.) – **Best Value + Highest Reviews**\n- **Capacity:** 150 seated dining / up to 300 standing (comfortably fits 100)\n- **Price:** €3,500 – €8,000 venue hire (one of the lowest in Paris)\n- **Reviews:** ⭐ 5.0 (37 reviews on Bridebook) – the highest-rated in this search\n- **Why:** Industrial-chic venue in the vibrant République district with exclusive use, in-house or external catering allowed, no corkage charge. Excellent combination of price, capacity flexibility, and stellar reviews.\n\n### 2. La Maison de Charly (Ternes) – **Exact 100-Guest Match + Low Price**\n- **Capacity:** Exactly **100** seated (150 reception)\n- **Price:** €4,000 – €6,000 full private hire\n- **Reviews:** "Excellent" on Tripadvisor (~59 reviews) with strong food/service praise\n- **Why:** Mediterranean restaurant that can be fully privatized for 50–100 guests — an exact match for your count at a very competitive price. Church within walking distance for ceremonies.\n\n### 3. Le Camondo (8th arr.) – **Lowest Starting Price + Exact Capacity**\n- **Capacity:** Exactly **100** guests\n- **Price:** €1,000 – €8,400 venue hire; packages €100–300/head\n- **Reviews:** No wedding reviews yet on Bridebook (newer venue)\n- **Why:** Beautiful listed mansion with a garden (can rent garden/veranda separately). The lowest starting price found. Note: less review history to verify quality.\n\n## 💎 Other Strong Contenders\n\n### 4. Bleu Seine (Barges on the Seine) – **Unique + Affordable**\n- **Capacity:** Fleet options fitting 100 (e.g., Tosca 20–110, Bistrot Alexandre III 10–130, Ivory 30–96)\n- **Price:** €3,000 – €7,500 venue hire; from ~€119 pp\n- **Reviews:** Moderate; a Parisian river-barge wedding with Eiffel Tower views — extremely memorable, fits the 100-guest mark with several boats.\n\n### 5. L\'Usine Deguerry (Paris)\n- **Capacity:** Exactly 100 guests\n- **Price:** €6,120 – €9,060\n- **Reviews:** ⭐ 5.0 (4 reviews)\n- **Why:** Perfect 100-guest capacity and perfect rating, though fewer reviews and a higher price than the top two.\n\n### 6. Le Clark Hotel (11th arr.) – **All-in-One Hotel Package**\n- **Capacity:** 50–100 guests\n- **Price:** €8,000–25,000+ total (2-night weekend incl. accommodation, ceremony €800–1,500, reception €65–120/head)\n- **Reviews:** ⭐ 4.9-rated hotel\n- **Why:** Everything under one roof (ceremony, dinner, rooms for guests) — great for out-of-town guests, at a moderate price.\n\n---\n\n## 💡 Recommendation Summary\nFor the **best balance of lowest price, exact 100-guest capacity, and highest reviews**, I\'d recommend:\n- **La Maison de Charly** (exact 100 capacity, €4,000–6,000, excellent reviews)\n- **La Fabrique République** (top-rated 5.0★, €3,500–8,000, fits 100 comfortably)\n\nIf you want the absolute lowest starting price, **Le Camondo** (from €1,000) is worth contacting, though it lacks review history.\n\n⚠️ Note: Palace hotels (Ritz, Crillon, Peninsula, Four Seasons, Plaza Athénée) also host 100 guests but are dramatically more expensive (typically €40,000–400,000+ total), so I\'ve excluded them from the top recommendations. Contact venues directly for seasonal quotes, as prices vary by date and package.', name='search_venues', id='9ddfac52-423a-4fae-ba52-422e64d8a18b', tool_call_id='call_4893ff2109724d27b85ab1dd'),
